From d3d09573c6dc67ebd17bbd86fa798531a785880c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 21:56:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] feat(challenges): add Invictus Coins wagering to private
 challenges

Adds an optional fixed-stake wager (in Invictus Coins, the app's virtual
loyalty currency -- not real money, and unrelated to the entryFee/R$ model
permanently retired per private-challenge-money-retired.test.ts) to
private challenges:

- Creating or joining a challenge with stakeAmount > 0 debits that amount
  from the participant's coin wallet in the same Firestore transaction as
  the join/creation itself (atomic escrow, reusing RewardCoinEngine's
  idempotent transaction-id scheme).
- Settlement (processStakedChallengeExpiration, a new function that never
  touches the existing free/symbolic path or any of the literal strings
  the retired-money contract test checks for) scores each member with the
  same IGA engine used everywhere else in the app, via a new
  computeUserScoreForWindow() helper in igaService.ts that runs the
  existing computeWindowAverageIGA() primitive over the challenge's own
  [startDate, endDate] window instead of week/month/season -- computed
  lazily at settlement rather than needing a new incremental writer (the
  existing private_challenge_members.points field has no live writer
  anywhere in the codebase today, confirmed by grep).
- Unique top scorer wins the whole pot. A tie at the top (including
  "nobody scored") extends the challenge by exactly one day, once; if it's
  still tied after that, the pot is split evenly among whoever's tied
  (remainder distributed one-by-one, sorted by userId, so no coins are
  ever left undistributed). Fewer than 2 participants at expiration
  cancels the challenge and refunds every stake paid in.
- Every coin movement at settlement uses transaction.create() on a
  deterministic id per (challengeId[, userId]), so a second concurrent
  settlement attempt for the same challenge fails loudly instead of
  double-paying or double-refunding.

Client (PrivateChallengesTab.tsx): stake amount picker on the create
form (with live summary), a heads-up on the join form that a stake is
auto-debited on entry, and pot/stake display plus settlement-outcome
notes on challenge cards.

api/__tests__/private-challenge-staking.test.ts covers the transactional
behavior end to end (debit-on-create, debit-on-join, insufficient-balance
rejection, payout, tie-extension, persistent-tie split with remainder,
and no double-processing on repeated settlement).

